WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.788
Cameras and network video recorders provide the visual source.

00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:07.887
Camera resolution, frame rate, field of view, low-light performance, placement,

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:11.575
and encoding influence both model accuracy and resource use.

00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:16.083
An NVR may aggregate streams and retain continuous or event video.

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:21.821
RTSP is a common method for delivering live video from cameras and video systems.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:25.919
The AI service connects to an authorized stream, decodes frames,

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:29.198
and samples them according to the use case.

00:00:29.198 --> 00:00:32.477
Stream credentials and network paths must be protected.

00:00:32.477 --> 00:00:36.165
A local server, workstation, or edge appliance runs inference.

00:00:36.165 --> 00:00:38.214
CPUs can handle lighter workloads,

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:43.542
while GPUs or dedicated accelerators improve throughput for larger models and more streams.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:48.460
Capacity planning should include decoding, inference, storage, dashboard use, and peak events.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.739
Vision models transform frames into detections, classifications, descriptions,

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:52.968
or activity observations.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:57.476
The surrounding software applies zones, thresholds, schedules, grouping, and business rules.

00:00:57.476 --> 00:01:01.984
Models and rules should be versioned so results can be reproduced.

00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:06.083
Storage may hold continuous video, event clips, thumbnails, model metadata,

00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:07.312
and review outcomes.

00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:11.411
Alerting channels deliver selected events to dashboards, email, mobile applications,

00:01:11.411 --> 00:01:13.050
or other approved systems.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.558
Logs record stream health, model errors, user activity, and configuration changes.

00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:22.886
The architecture should show every data flow and trust boundary: camera, network, NVR,

00:01:22.886 --> 00:01:26.164
inference host, storage, dashboard, alert channel, and administrator.

00:01:26.164 --> 00:01:29.853
Reliable time and camera identity let reviewers correlate events.

00:01:29.853 --> 00:01:32.722
Monitoring health is part of the product,

00:01:32.722 --> 00:01:36.820
because a silent camera or stalled model creates false confidence.
